The Porsche 944 S was produced from 1987 to 1988 [2, 3, 7]. It featured a 2.5L 16-valve engine producing 187-190 hp and 170 lb-ft of torque [2, 3, 4, 7, 9, 10]. 0-60 mph was around 7.0-7.7 seconds [2, 4, 13, 17]. Top speed was around 142 mph [2, 7, 9, 10, 17]. It was rear-wheel drive and typically came with a 5-speed manual transmission [4, 9]. Ground clearance was around 4.9 inches [5, 8, 14, 16]. Turning radius is listed as 33.8 ft in one source [35]. MPG is estimated around 19-28 combined [4, 7, 9, 17, 19, 25, 26, 28]. Cargo space is around 11.2 cu ft [35]. Rear seats are very small [2, 3, 34]. ABS and airbags were optional on the 944 S, standard on the Turbo [2, 6, 23, 29]. Handling and steering are generally praised [20, 21]. Reliability is dependent on maintenance due to age [11, 18, 20, 21, 24].

